verses.commentary:
2:13 "wisdom excels folly as light excels darkness" There is value in wisdom, but it is not ultimate (cf. Eccl. 7:11,12,19;
9:18; 10:10). Human wisdom is always tenuous and partial.

▣ The NASB translation has left out the significant term "profit" or "advantage" (BDB 452, KB 404). See note at Eccl. 1:3.
